# MACHINE.md

Facts about one specific computer, for an agent that is about to change something on it. Copy this template to `~/.config/agents/MACHINE.md` on Linux and macOS, or `%USERPROFILE%\.config\agents\MACHINE.md` on Windows, then fill it by running [bootstrap-machine.prompt.md](bootstrap-machine.prompt.md) in any agent.

The file is not loaded into every session. The global instruction file (`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, which Codex, OpenCode, Kilo Code and Copilot reach through their own links) carries one line pointing here, so an agent reads it only when the task touches the machine itself:

```text
Before changing disks, mounts, boot, drivers, audio, displays, system packages or services on this computer, read ~/.config/agents/MACHINE.md, and add a change log entry to it for anything you change.
```

Rules for whoever edits this file:

1. Every row carries the command or the person it came from and the date it was true. A fact with no source is a guess.
2. Facts the owner stated and no command can confirm are marked `owner` in the Source column. A later discovery run never overwrites them silently. It records a disagreement under Known quirks instead.
3. Anything that needs root to read is listed under Needs root as a command for the owner. An agent never runs it.
4. No secret goes in here: no password, recovery key, Wi-Fi passphrase, token or serial number of a credential device.
5. The never-touch list is the most important table in the file. Read it before any storage command.

Last full discovery: `<YYYY-MM-DD>` by `<agent and version>` on `<OS and version>`.

