| Device | Model | Size | Bus | Partition | Filesystem | Label or UUID | Encryption | Mount point | Source | Verified |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `<nvme0n1>` | `<model>` | `<size>` | `<nvme, sata, usb>` | `<p1>` | `<fs>` | `<label>`, `<uuid>` | `<none, LUKS, BitLocker, FileVault>` | `<path or unmounted>` | | |

Mount table, as written in `/etc/fstab` or its platform equivalent:

```text
<paste the non-comment fstab lines>
```

Never touch. No agent mounts, unlocks, repairs, formats, partitions, writes to or adds to fstab any of these, for any reason, without the owner asking in the current conversation:

| Device | Why | Source |
|---|---|---|
| `<sdX1>` | `<BitLocker, holds the owner's data>` | owner |

